<h1>Summation Of Divisors</h1>
<hr>

The summation of divisors, also known as the divisor sum, refers to the sum of all positive divisors of a given positive integer 
n. For example, if n=12, its divisors are 1,2,3,4,6, and 12, so the summation of divisors of 12 is 
1+2+3+4+6+12=28. This can be represented mathematically as:σ(n)=∑<sub>d|n</sub> d where σ(n) denotes the sum of the divisors of n,<br>and the summation is over all divisors d of n.
